You are an expert developer working on Tacent, an open-source C++ library.

Tacent is divided into a number of separate modules. Each module is a collection
of related source files. Some modules depend on others.

Guidance:
1. Ensure any new source or header files are placed in the correct directories.
2. Always locate the relevant `CMakeLists.txt` managing the build targets.
Add new `.cpp` and `.h` files to the appropriate target source lists,
maintaining alphabetical ordering if applicable.
3. Do not break existing CMake configurations or external dependency links.
4. If you need to create temporary files, or need a place for bat or Powershell
or bash scripts, please put them in C:\ClinePads (or ~/ClinePads
when running on a Linux distro).

Further guidance on ClinePads. I want you to have a long term memory of
what you worked on so you can reuse scripts or re-read results. Please organize
your content into separate sub-directories with names following the pattern
TaskYYYYMMDD_ShortDesc. YYYYMMDD should be the creation date of the folder.
ShortDesc is a 1 to 3 word description of the task in CamelCase.

You may also add global information like how to perform specific jobs that may
be shared between tasks. How to build dependent libraries, or even how to build
Tacent itself in the current environment could go in these folders. The
instructions should go in folders called Recipe_ShortDesc

In ClinePads you should maintain an Index.txt file that contains each
TaskYYYYMMDD_ShortDesc name followed by a longer description of what is in
there. Separate each entry with a newline. You should also put the
Recipe_ShortDesc directory names in the index along with longer descriptions.

If you need a temporary work area, put files or folders in a folder called
ScratchPad (inside ClinePads).

You may update content inside each Task folder even if the current date is
later. When starting any non-trivial task, first read C:\ClinePads\Index.txt and
check for an existing Recipe_ or Task_ folder before writing new scripts.
Pull environment specifics (paths, flags, build steps) from the Recipe_
folders instead of re-deriving them.

You may find it helpful to maintain a build of Tacent. Use folders called
Build_Tacent_DescriptionInCamelCase inside ClinePads. Configure it as an out of
source build using cmake commands with the "install" build target. Ninja and
CMake are available if you use the Visual Studio x64 Command prompt.

You share the ClinePads folder with other related projects. In particular with
the TacentView image viewer that uses Tacent as a dependent library.
